**SAE Report Form and Mandatory Logs (Section 8.5.2)**

2. The SAE Report Form must be included in the e-CRF system and completed per instructions. The following logs are mandatory for initial and follow-up SAE reports:
   - Demographics
   - Adverse Event Log
   - Medical History Log
   - Concomitant Medication Log
[Section 8.5.2 Collection, Recording and Reporting of Serious Adverse Events SAE Reporting by the Investigator · p.63]

**General e-CRF System Requirements (Section 10.2)**

3. The e-CRF must support electronic signature/authorisation by the Investigator for each patient's entries, audit trail tracking (including date, time, and name of person making corrections), and timely data entry following patient visits or data availability.
[Section 10.2 Electronic Case Record Form · p.71]

**Protocol Deviation Documentation (Section 12.2)**

4. Any protocol deviation must be documented in (or included in) e-CRF data, accompanied by a description of the deviation, relevant dates (start and stop), and the action taken.
